(Topic 1: IP Addressing) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
18 TL
1 0 0 1 54 706 Tm
(An IP address identifies a network interface and helps routers) Tj
T*
(direct packets to a destination. IPv4 uses 32 bits, typically) Tj
T*
(formatted as four decimal numbers \(e.g., 192.168.1.1\). IPv6 uses 128) Tj
T*
(bits, represented in hexadecimal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each IPv4 decimal number represents an 8-bit octet and ranges from 0) Tj
T*
(to 255. The four octets together account for the 32 bits in an IPv4) Tj
T*
(address.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A router examines the destination IP address when choosing where to) Tj
T*
(forward a packet. An address tells the network where to deliver) Tj
T*
(data; it does not describe the contents of that data.) Tj
ET
endstream
