(Topic 2: DNS) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
18 TL
1 0 0 1 54 706 Tm
(DNS translates human-readable domain names into IP addresses. For) Tj
T*
(example, a fictional lookup for study.example can return 192.0.2.25) Tj
T*
(to the client.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A DNS resolver receives a name lookup from a client and obtains the) Tj
T*
(requested record. An A record contains an IPv4 address. An AAAA) Tj
T*
(record contains an IPv6 address.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A DNS cache keeps a previous lookup result for the record's time to) Tj
T*
(live \(TTL\). Reusing an unexpired cached answer avoids another) Tj
T*
(lookup. Once that lifetime expires, the resolver must obtain a) Tj
T*
(current answer rather than treating the expired entry as fresh.) Tj
ET
endstream
