1 0 0 1 54 706 Tm
(HTTP is an application-layer protocol used to exchange requests and) Tj
T*
(responses. In its client-server model, a client sends a request and) Tj
T*
(a server returns a response.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A GET request asks for a representation of a resource. In this) Tj
T*
(synthetic example, GET /notes requests the study notes stored at the) Tj
T*
(/notes path. A POST request submits data to a resource for) Tj
T*
(processing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(An HTTP response includes a status code and may include a body.) Tj
T*
(Status code 200 means the request succeeded. Status code 404 means) Tj
T*
(the requested resource was not found. The client can use the status) Tj
T*
(code to distinguish a successful /notes response from a missing) Tj
T*
(resource.) Tj
ET
